{
  "id": 461966991,
  "iid": 23807,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "OPCUA: Coverity dereference after null check",
  "description": "proto_tree_add_item_ret_string_and_length() doesn't allow the length\nreturn value pointer to be NULL. (But does allow the string value\npointer.) Since the path where it's called has already checked that\nthe length is positive (and set the length return value to the\ninitial length), the return value is always the same as the provided\nvalue, so we can just call proto_tree_add_item_ret_string().\n\nCoverity CID 1548330\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
